// PBM - Hello World! :: RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   colour     : not assigned by Linguist
//   layer      : full (byte-balanced rainbow bar)
//   upstream   : https://github.com/quxianp/RAiNBOW_Hello-World
//   reference  : see https://esolangs.org/ and https://rosettacode.org/

# A real binary PBM (P4). Rows are padded to whole bytes, so a 12-bit row
# still occupies two. "Hello World!" is the comment.
0000  50 34 0A 23 20 48 65 6C 6C 6F 20 57 6F 72 6C 64 |P4.# Hello World|
0010  21 0A 31 32 20 31 0A 0A 0A                      |!.12 1...|
